# Generated coverage artifacts — never commit
coverage/

# Fleet project profile — machine-specific, never shared.
# project-profile.md is GENERATED by the /fleet-init skill and pins absolute
# paths for one checkout (e.g. /Users/<name>/...). Committing it means the next
# clone inherits another machine.s paths, every agent greps a path that does not
# resolve, and the misses get reported as defects. Run /fleet-init after cloning
# to regenerate it. The TEMPLATE beside it stays tracked — this pattern is the
# exact filename, so project-profile.template.md is deliberately unaffected.
project-profile.md

# Ad-hoc coverage dumps (coverage-full/, coverage-full2/ …). 18.4 MB of these
# reached a PR on 2026-09-23; `coverage/` alone did not catch the variants.
/coverage-*/

# Playwright run output (last-run state, traces, screenshots).
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# Local scratch: redirected test/coverage runs and other one-off output.
# Kept on disk for the person who made it, never committed.
/.local-artifacts/

# Playwright focus-contrast proof output (report JSON + screenshots).
/e2e/artifacts/

# Office lock files
~$*
